title: Event stream (NDJSON)
section: Reference
desc: The versioned stream of events a run produces, which every report is built from: types, fields and an example.
lede: Everything that happens in a run is an event. The NDJSON reporter writes them one JSON object per line. All other reporters, the debugger and the history tooling read only this stream.
---
<h2>Write it</h2>
<cb lang="bash">$ npx bddr -f ndjson:reports/events.ndjson</cb>
<p>Each line has a <code>ts</code> (milliseconds since the epoch) and a <code>type</code>. The stream is at schema version 1. Adding an optional field is not a breaking change. Renaming or removing a field or an event type bumps the version.</p>

<h2>An example</h2>
<cb lang="json" title="reports/events.ndjson (shortened)">{"ts":1794727537708,"type":"runStarted","runId":"2a6e4947-...","schemaVersion":1,"framework":{"name":"bddr","version":"0.1.0"},"runtime":{"name":"node","version":"v22.23.4"},"dryRun":false}
{"ts":1794727537708,"type":"specParsed","uri":"features/checkout.feature","featureName":"Checkout","scenarioCount":4,"errors":[]}
{"ts":1794727537936,"type":"scenarioFinished","scenarioId":"create-user","attempt":1,"status":"passed","durationMs":27}</cb>

<h2>Event types</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Fields</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>runStarted</code></td><td><code>runId</code>, <code>schemaVersion</code>, <code>framework</code>, <code>runtime</code>, <code>dryRun</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>specParsed</code></td><td><code>uri</code>, <code>featureName</code>, <code>scenarioCount</code>, <code>errors</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>planReady</code></td><td><code>scenarios</code> (id, name, uri, line, tags, steps, example row, groups, dependencies), <code>workers</code>, <code>groups</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>workerStarted</code></td><td><code>workerId</code>, <code>pid</code>, <code>startupMs</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>groupStarted</code>, <code>groupFinished</code></td><td><code>group</code>, <code>attempt</code>, and <code>status</code> when finished</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>groupRetrying</code></td><td><code>group</code>, <code>attempt</code>, <code>scenarioIds</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>featureStarted</code>, <code>featureFinished</code></td><td><code>uri</code>, <code>name</code>, and <code>status</code> when finished</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>hookStarted</code>, <code>hookFinished</code></td><td><code>hookId</code>, <code>hookName</code>, <code>level</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>scenarioId</code>, and <code>status</code>, <code>durationMs</code>, <code>error</code> when finished</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>scenarioStarted</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>attempt</code>, <code>workerId</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>stepStarted</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>stepId</code>, <code>keyword</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>line</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>stepFinished</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>stepId</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>durationMs</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>definition</code> (pattern, location), <code>snippet</code> for undefined steps, <code>mode</code> and <code>attempts</code> for repeated or retried steps</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>stepAttemptFinished</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>stepId</code>, <code>attempt</code>, <code>of</code>, <code>mode</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>durationMs</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>attachment</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>stepId</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>mediaType</code>, <code>encoding</code> (<code>identity</code> or <code>base64</code>), <code>body</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>log</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>message</code>, <code>level</code>, <code>source</code> (<code>user</code> or <code>bddr</code>), <code>data</code>, <code>attempt</code>, <code>attachment</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>scenarioFinished</code></td><td><code>scenarioId</code>, <code>attempt</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>durationMs</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>willRetry</code>, <code>flaky</code>, <code>quarantined</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>runFinished</code></td><td><code>success</code>, <code>summary</code> (scenario and step counts per status, <code>durationMs</code>, <code>flaky</code>, <code>quarantined</code>, <code>retried</code>), <code>error</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>A status is one of <code>passed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>skipped</code>, <code>pending</code>, <code>undefined</code> or <code>ambiguous</code>. An error has <code>message</code> and optional <code>name</code> and <code>stack</code>.</p>

<h2>Use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Re-run what failed:</strong> <code>npx bddr --rerun-failed reports/events.ndjson</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Merge runs:</strong> <code>npx bddr report a.ndjson b.ndjson -f html:reports/merged.html</code>. Later runs win.</li>
  <li><strong>Colour the living documentation:</strong> <code>npx bddr docs --results reports/events.ndjson</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Read it yourself:</strong> one line per event, so <code>jq</code> or a few lines of Node.js will do. For example, to list failed scenarios:</li>
</ul>
<cb lang="bash">$ jq -r 'select(.type=="scenarioFinished" and .status=="failed") | .scenarioId' reports/events.ndjson</cb>
<aside class="callout note"><p class="callout-title">Compatibility</p><p>The events map one to one onto Cucumber Messages. <code>-f messages</code> produces them. Scenarios generated from <code>@data</code> files are left out, and hooks are not emitted as hook messages yet.</p></aside>
